test_ddl_deparse is an example of how to use the pg_ddl_command datatype.
It is not intended to do anything useful on its own; rather, it is a
demonstration of how to use the datatype, and to provide some unit tests for
it.

The functions in this extension are intended to be able to process some
part of the struct and produce some readable output, preferably handling
all possible cases so that SQL test code can be written.

The module also tests the DDL deparser.  With
test_ddl_deparse.execute_deparsed_ddl on, each supported command is run in
a subtransaction that is rolled back, deparsed from a ddl_command_end event
trigger, and the deparsed command is executed instead.
test_ddl_deparse.print_deparsed_ddl prints the deparsed command as a
NOTICE, and test_ddl_deparse.log_declined_commands logs the commands the
deparser does not support.  t/001_deparse_regress.pl runs the core
regression tests this way.
